1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,520
No, see, the way it's set
now, the gyro's too sensitive.

2
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,497
If you want to prioritize
the visual tracking,

3
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:12,917
you gotta give yourself a little
more room in these parameters.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,417
Okay, but won't it lag like crazy
if she makes any sudden moves?

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,477
I guess you'll just have to trust that the

6
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,619
learning program and the
optimizer can deal with it.

7
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,400
How much longer, guys?

8
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,485
Our lunch break's almost over!

9
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:29,277
Let's just save this as the
default setting and hope it works.

10
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,880
Hey, uh, Yuki, can you hear okay?

11
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:34,180
Yep, I hear you loud and clear.

12
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:35,860
Good, all right.

13
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,557
I'm firing up the lens now,
so it might get bright.

14
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,437
Let me know when you can see perfect,
and I'll lock that setting in.

15
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,350
Fire away!

16
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:46,510
Hold it!

17
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:48,731
Okay, you're ready to go.

18
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:53,046
Last thing, I installed stabilizers,
but they're kind of janky.

19
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,897
Try not to make any sudden moves, okay?

20
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:56,240
Ah, thanks, Kirito!

21
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:17,420
Thank you.

22
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:34,040
That's why I can't hear you.

23
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:42,240
The story of the story is
the beginning of the song.

24
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:56,980
I'm going to connect with you.

25
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,400
Oh, give it for my way.

26
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:32,850
Wow!

27
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:34,260
Your school's ginormous!

28
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,540
I know, right?

29
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,157
I'm sorry I couldn't
show you around first,

30
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:40,877
but the lunch break's almost over
and we don't want to be late.

31
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:41,960
Nah, that's okay.

32
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:45,040
I'm just excited to check
out your class. Sweet.

33
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:49,360
Then let's head to the faculty room
and introduce you to my teacher.

34
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,130
What's wrong?

35
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,952
It's the one part of school I don't miss.

36
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:56,740
Go into the faculty room.

37
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,000
Don't worry.

38
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:00,157
The teachers here aren't
your typical teachers.

39
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:01,070
They're cool.

40
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:02,540
Excuse me!

41
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:03,920
Me too!

42
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:08,684
I just wanted to make
sure it was still alright.

43
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,720
Sure, I'm fine with it.

44
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:14,657
And what's the name of the student
who'll be joining us today?

45
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:16,220
Oh, um, Yuki!

46
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,580
Yuki Kono, sir!

47
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:19,720
Uh, okay.

48
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:22,957
Miss Kono, you're welcome in
my class any time you want.

49
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:26,057
Although, we start
Akutagawa's alori today.

50
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:29,057
Unless you stick with it to the
end, you won't get the point!

51
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:31,840
Yes, sir, thank you very much.

52
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,280
See you in class.

53
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:59,657
What's that, Miss Yuki?

54
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,857
Hey, how'd you know my name?

55
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:04,837
Oh, no, she was using my last name there.

56
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:05,857
Oh, right.

57
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:09,117
Uh, guys, meet Yuki Kono.

58
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:12,137
She's in the hospital right
now and can't leave her room.

59
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:14,617
So instead, she'll be
attending our class like this.

60
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:15,797
Nice to meet you.

61
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,300
I can only hang out for?

62
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:19,650
a little while though.

63
00:04:19,733 --> 00:04:20,700
Nice to meet you.

64
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,900
Hey there, my name's Cait. Oh, hi.

65
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:25,000
Hey, nice to meet you too.

66
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:41,017
Please stand. Bow. Be seated.

67
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,760
All right then, class.

68
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,600
Please open your textbooks to page 97.

69
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:49,560
We'll be reading Alori
by Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

70
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:52,280
Let's see, who'll read it for us?

71
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:55,300
Yuki Kono, would you do the honors?

72
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:58,090
Me?

73
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:01,810
Problem?

74
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,090
No, sir.

75
00:05:03,173 --> 00:05:04,100
I can do it.

76
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,820
Yuki, are you up for this?

77
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:13,100
I might not look it,
but I have read before.

78
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,880
When Ryohei was eight years old,

79
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:26,022
construction on the light railway
between Odawara and Atami began.

80
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:31,075
Every day, he would head to the
outskirts of town to watch the progress.

81
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:35,097
It wasn't the construction of
it that fascinated him so much.

82
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:39,239
It was the sight of the lorries
transporting the soil which drew him.

83
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,492
There were two laborers aboard the lorry,

84
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:45,228
standing behind the
soil they'd just loaded.

85
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:50,417
Since the lorry was headed down the
mountain, it didn't need anyone to push it.

86
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:54,800
So as the chassis swung, and the
sleeves of the laborer's coats flapped,

87
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:57,560
and the narrow rails
bent under the strain,

88
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:03,160
Ryohei would gaze longingly at these
sights and wish he could be a laborer too.

89
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:08,560
Or at the very least, be able to
ride on it with them, if only once.

90
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:16,177
I love listening to you read Yuki.

91
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:18,517
Hey, have you had a
chance to tour the school?

92
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,277
If not, we could show you around.

93
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,817
Take it easy, guys.

94
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:23,357
Hey, wanna go to a soccer match?

95
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:24,557
Thanks, guys.

96
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:25,700
You're the best.

97
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,197
Now that was fun.

98
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,557
I know, right?

99
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:32,517
Thanks for making today happen. Asuna.

100
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,937
Really, I had a blast.

101
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:36,177
I'm never.

102
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:38,080
gonna forget today. Ever.

103
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:43,760
Well, of course you won't.

104
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:46,391
The teacher said you could come back again

105
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:47,670
if you want.

106
00:06:47,753 --> 00:06:49,717
Oh, modern Japanese is
third period tomorrow.

107
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,630
You don't

108
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:51,850
want to miss that.

109
00:06:51,933 --> 00:06:53,240
Yeah. Okay, what's next?

110
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:55,997
Is there anything else
you want to do or see?

111
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,560
Oh, um,

112
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,077
I guess there is one?

113
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,100
place I'd like to go. Where?

114
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:10,317
It's so pretty here huh?

115
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,337
Just look at that sky!

116
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,977
Yeah.

117
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:15,037
Hey!

118
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:17,437
Are your folks cool with
you staying out so late?

119
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,437
You've been hauling me around all day!

120
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,217
Don't you worry about it!

121
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:22,157
I send them a text!

122
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,457
And it's fine! Well!

123
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:24,897
Where do you want to go next?

124
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:25,810
Yuki!

125
00:07:25,893 --> 00:07:26,723
Go left!

126
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:46,060
Hey, are we in Tsukimidai yet?

127
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,030
Yeah.

128
00:07:48,113 --> 00:07:49,719
Next corner, there's a white house.

129
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,078
Can you stop there?

130
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:02,200
Yuki, this is your house, huh?

131
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:03,690
Mm-hmm.

132
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:07,100
I never thought I'd get
the chance to see it again.

133
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:10,202
Thanks for bringing me out here.

134
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:11,658
And for everything.

135
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,231
Do you want to go inside?

136
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,980
Nah, this was enough.

137
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:20,197
Come on, let's head back
before your folks get worried.

138
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,280
No, it's okay.

139
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,147
We can stay a little longer.

140
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:29,497
Me and my family, we only got to
live here a little over a year.

141
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:34,000
And the weird thing is, I can
remember every day so clear.

142
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:38,557
My sister and me used to play in
the yard, running around and around.

143
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:42,581
We had barbecues, and we even built
these bookshelves with our dad.

144
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:44,000
Good times.

145
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:45,940
Lucky you.

146
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:47,970
Yeah.

147
00:08:48,053 --> 00:08:49,597
They're gonna tear it all down, though.

148
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:50,940
Really? Why?

149
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:55,097
My aunt wants to either put a
convenience store here, or maybe sell it.

150
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:56,040
No way.

151
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:59,957
That's why I wanted to come here,
so I could see it one more time.

152
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,420
Well, I know how you can save it. How?

153
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,440
You're 15 now, aren't you?

154
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,200
When you turn 16, find someone
you love and marry him.

155
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,457
That way you'll have
someone around who will

156
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:13,011
keep this house from ever being torn down.

157
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:16,360
You got the craziest ideas.

158
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:20,877
I don't think there's anyone
I want to marry, though.

159
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:21,790
Oh, yeah?

160
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:23,737
But you and June make a cute couple.

161
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:24,760
God, no.

162
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:26,520
That guy's so immature.

163
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,580
Let's see.

164
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,260
Who should I marry?

165
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,500
Oh, I know. You.

166
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:36,477
The only thing is, if you marry
me, you'll have to be the wife.

167
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:40,980
I mean, the other way around, my name'd
be Yuki Yuki, and that'd be weird.

168
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:45,840
I can't imagine what my mom
would say. I know. I'm kidding.

169
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,880
Besides, you already got someone lined up.

170
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:51,720
Oh, yeah, I guess.

171
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,666
Still, you should be careful.

172
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:56,957
I get the feeling he's not
living in the real world either.

173
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,680
Not like me, but, you know.

174
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,682
I can't thank you enough, Asuna.

175
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,137
Just to stay in my old house again?

176
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:07,514
You don't know how happy that makes me.

177
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:13,280
Back when we lived here, I remember
we'd go to church to pray and stuff.

178
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:16,519
And Mom used to always say
this to me and my sister.

179
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:19,457
God would never put us through all this

180
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:22,460
suffering if He didn't
think we could bear it.

181
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,831
It didn't make me feel any better, though.

182
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:28,817
Instead of quoting the Bible,

183
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:33,018
what I really wanted was for Mom to
talk to us like, well, like a mom.

184
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:38,980
But you know, after seeing her old
house again, I think I get it now.

185
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:41,032
The words didn't matter.

186
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:43,535
It was the feeling behind those words.

187
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,877
She was praying for me so I
wouldn't feel sorry for myself,

188
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:52,540
so I could be strong to the
end, and now I finally get it.

189
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:55,740
I'm the same.

190
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:57,057
See, I...

191
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:59,760
I haven't understood my mom, either.

192
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:03,662
I can't hear what she's
really trying to tell me.

193
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,980
She can't seem to hear me.

194
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,029
Remember what you told me?

195
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:12,732
That sometimes you have to
fight to get your point across?

196
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:15,600
How can I get to be strong? Like you?

197
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:17,970
Me?

198
00:11:18,053 --> 00:11:19,960
I'm not strong. No way.

199
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:21,460
Oh, yes, you are.

200
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:22,857
You're not like me.

201
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:26,777
When you stand up to someone, you don't
flinch or let them intimidate you.

202
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,817
Nothing seems to scare you at all.

203
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:30,782
It's like second nature for you.

204
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,480
Yeah, I don't know.

205
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:37,257
When I was living in the real
world, or you know what I mean,

206
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:39,281
most of the time I was faking it.

207
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:42,957
It's like I thought I had
to act cheerful because I

208
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:46,040
didn't want to make my mom
and dad feel sad for me.

209
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,170
Yuki.

210
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:50,392
You want to know what I think in the end?

211
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,108
So what if I'm just acting?

212
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:54,677
If I get to spend more time smiling,

213
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:57,760
even if it's fake, what's
the big deal, am I right?

214
00:11:58,040 --> 00:12:01,320
I mean, it's not like I got
a whole lot of time left.

215
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:06,109
And it'd be a shame to waste whatever
I do got by moping around all the time.

216
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,247
So now I say exactly
what I feel to everyone.

217
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:12,177
And if they got a problem
with that, who cares?

218
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:13,907
At least they spoke my mind.

219
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,780
And maybe even got a
little closer to them.

220
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:18,650
You're right.

221
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:20,857
That's the reason we're here today.

222
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:21,770
Why?

223
00:12:21,853 --> 00:12:23,800
Why we're so close after only a few days?

224
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:25,392
It's all because of you.

225
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:26,750
Nope.

226
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:27,909
That wasn't because of me.

227
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:32,640
It's because even after I ran away
from you, you tracked me down.

228
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:37,985
Look, how about you try talking
to your mom, like you did to me?

229
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:42,359
If you try telling her how you feel,
maybe you'll get through to her.

230
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:45,960
Don't worry. You can do it.

231
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,720
You're way stronger than me. Honest.

232
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:53,690
Yuki...

233
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:57,240
You hit me with everything you had.

234
00:12:57,660 --> 00:13:00,377
That's how I knew I could trust
you with everything I had.

235
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:03,640
In the end, it worked out
for both of us, didn't it?

236
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,140
Yes, it did.

237
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:06,980
Thank you so much, Yuki.

238
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:27,859
If you try telling her how you feel,
maybe you'll get through to her.

239
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:32,000
Don't worry, I know you can do it!

240
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,190
Come in.

241
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:51,999
You're late again.

242
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,100
I'm sorry.

243
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:57,989
Well, if you're hungry, you'll have to
make do with whatever's in the fridge.

244
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:02,657
Oh, and don't forget, the deadline for
your transfer application is due tomorrow.

245
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:04,916
Make sure it's filled out by morning.

246
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,720
Actually, about that …

247
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:10,900
We need to talk, Mother.

248
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:13,240
Well, what is it?

249
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:15,264
I can't really explain it here.

250
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,546
Okay then, where shall we go?

251
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,940
The virtual world.

252
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:27,376
It'll only be for a little while,
and you're going to have to use this.

253
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:30,396
Don't be ridiculous!

254
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:33,737
If you can't tell me what this
is about like a normal person,

255
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:35,037
I don't want to hear it.

256
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,377
But you don't understand!

257
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,317
It's the only way I can explain!

258
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,753
It's just five minutes!

259
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:42,200
Mom, please!

260
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:46,317
There's no other way to tell you what
I'm thinking and how I'm feeling, honest!

261
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,400
I can't tell you any of that here!

262
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,037
Just this once!

263
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:53,140
Mom, all I want is for
you to see my world!

264
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:01,120
Five minutes.

265
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:05,440
But, no matter what you say,

266
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:09,237
I have no intention of allowing you
to attend that school again next year,

267
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,150
understood?

268
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:13,751
Also, once you're done, you
will fill out that application.

269
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,010
Okay.

270
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:17,460
So how do I use that thing?

271
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:24,240
Just sit back and relax.

272
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:29,326
Once I turn it on, it'll automatically
connect you to my subaccount in the game.

273
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,986
After you're in, wait for me.

274
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:35,134
I'm turning it on now.

275
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:47,400
Link, start!

276
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,100
This is so bizarre.

277
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:09,500
Seeing a strange face mimic
what I do is unsettling.

278
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:12,540
And this body, it's so light.

279
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:13,859
Oh, that's normal.

280
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:17,844
That particular avatar's weight
setting is about 90 pounds or so.

281
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:20,037
Feels lighter than your real body, huh?

282
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,600
That is so rude.

283
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:24,192
I do not appreciate what you're implying.

284
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:25,738
That's interesting.

285
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:28,297
Your face here looks
just like your real one.

286
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:29,460
Well, yes.

287
00:16:30,460 --> 00:16:31,897
Actually, I take it back.

288
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:34,217
Your real face is puffier than this one.

289
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:35,880
Oh, now who's being rude?

290
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:38,119
I look the same here as I do there.

291
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:43,780
Well, I'm here. Now what?

292
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,977
You don't have much time left.

293
00:16:46,060 --> 00:16:46,942
Follow me, Mom.

294
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:17,990
You see?

295
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:19,277
It looks just like it.

296
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:21,680
I have no idea what you mean.

297
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:24,020
All I see is some old cedar gro -

298
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:27,904
Doesn't it bring back memories?

299
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:30,591
Of the house that grandma and grandpa had?

300
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:37,697
I really loved their place in Miyagi.

301
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:39,200
It was magical.

302
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:08,140
Remember that Obon holiday when I was 12?

303
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:12,480
You, Dad, and Koichiro went to
the Yuki family Kampan in Kyoto,

304
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,624
and I went to Miyagi by myself.

305
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:16,177
I remember.

306
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:20,640
When I got there, I apologized to
them that you couldn't be with us.

307
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:24,300
I felt bad you couldn't
visit our ancestors' graves.

308
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:29,360
I wanted to, but that year, the Yukis
were having an important memorial service.

309
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,132
No, Mom, I'm not blaming you or anything.

310
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:35,900
In fact, you know what Grandpa said?

311
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:40,140
He said not to fuss because he
and Grandma were so proud of you.

312
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,510
Huh?

313
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,334
You left this village,

314
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:49,617
went to university, became a
scholar and got your work published.

315
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:53,818
It made him so happy to see you make
a name for yourself in the world!

316
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:58,064
And then he told me
something I'll never forget.

317
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:01,597
That someday you might get tired from all

318
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:04,137
the hard work you do and
need a break from it.

319
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:05,880
And if that day ever came,

320
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:09,457
he said he wanted to make sure the house
and the mountain were always there.

321
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:11,217
That he'd guard them.

322
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:13,517
To give you a place to come home to.

323
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:14,900
if you needed it.

324
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,257
I didn't understand it then!

325
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:25,977
But now, after everything
that's happened to me?

326
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:27,340
I think I finally do.

327
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:32,051
Life isn't just about doing
the things that make you happy?

328
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:34,397
It's also about finding a way to live.

329
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,737
Where the happiness of
everyone around you?

330
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:37,940
fulfills you too.

331
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:41,430
Somehow,

332
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:45,851
I want to figure out how to live a life
that makes everyone around me happy.

333
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:48,597
I want a life that lets
me be there for the people

334
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:51,445
I care about when they
need someone to lean on.

335
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:52,960
That's all I want.

336
00:19:54,140 --> 00:19:56,260
Mother, I'll study and work hard,

337
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:59,400
but I want to keep going
to the school that I love.

338
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:25,440
What is this?

339
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:26,900
This is crazy.

340
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,494
I'm not really crying.

341
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:34,080
Mom, you can't hide it when
you're sad in this world.

342
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,980
When you cry, you cry,
just like in real life.

343
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:41,680
Such an annoying world.

344
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:26,394
Asuna, are you determined to live the
kind of selfless life you spoke of?

345
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:29,290
Fine.

346
00:21:29,373 --> 00:21:33,927
If that is what you want, you'll have to
be strong enough to carry that burden.

347
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,980
So make sure you go to college.

348
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:42,351
And for that, you'll have to get better
grades this trimester and next year.

349
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:45,430
Really?

350
00:21:45,513 --> 00:21:46,920
Then I can stay?

351
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:48,260
That's up to you.

352
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,445
You'll have to prove yourself.

353
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,240
Do your best.

354
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:02,060
Thanks, Mom. I will.

355
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:05,420
Thank you, Yuki.

356
00:22:11,760 --> 00:22:13,340
Here I go.

357
00:22:14,140 --> 00:22:14,970
Thank you

358
